# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Background {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Fermi-Hubbard model describes electrons hopping on a lattice with an energy penalty for double occupancy. On a one-dimensional chain of $L$ sites with open boundaries, the Hamiltonian is defined as follows:\n"
msgstr "Inilalarawan ng Fermi-Hubbard model ang mga electron na tumatalon sa isang lattice na may energy penalty para sa double occupancy. Sa isang one-dimensional na chain ng $L$ site na may open boundary, ganito ang depinisyon ng Hamiltonian:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = -\\sum_{i=0}^{L-2} \\sum_{\\sigma \\in \\{\\uparrow,\\downarrow\\}} t_{h,i} \\left( c^\\dagger_{i\\sigma} c_{i+1,\\sigma} + \\mathrm{h.c.} \\right) + \\sum_{i=0}^{L-1} U_i\\, n_{i\\uparrow} n_{i\\downarrow} - \\sum_{i=0}^{L-1} \\sum_\\sigma \\mu_i\\, n_{i\\sigma},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = -\\sum_{i=0}^{L-2} \\sum_{\\sigma \\in \\{\\uparrow,\\downarrow\\}} t_{h,i} \\left( c^\\dagger_{i\\sigma} c_{i+1,\\sigma} + \\mathrm{h.c.} \\right) + \\sum_{i=0}^{L-1} U_i\\, n_{i\\uparrow} n_{i\\downarrow} - \\sum_{i=0}^{L-1} \\sum_\\sigma \\mu_i\\, n_{i\\sigma},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $c^\\dagger_{i\\sigma}$ creates a fermion of spin $\\sigma$ on site $i$ and $n_{i\\sigma} = c^\\dagger_{i\\sigma} c_{i\\sigma}$ counts them. The three terms are the hopping amplitude $t_{h,i}$ on the bond between sites $i$ and $i+1$, the on-site interaction $U_i$, and the chemical potential $\\mu_i$. The tutorial measures energy in units of $t_h$ and time in units of $1/t_h$.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $c^\\dagger_{i\\sigma}$ ay lumilikha ng fermion na may spin $\\sigma$ sa site $i$ at ang $n_{i\\sigma} = c^\\dagger_{i\\sigma} c_{i\\sigma}$ ay nagbibilang sa kanila. Ang tatlong term ay ang hopping amplitude $t_{h,i}$ sa bond sa pagitan ng mga site na $i$ at $i+1$, ang on-site interaction na $U_i$, at ang chemical potential na $\\mu_i$. Sinusukat ng tutorial ang energy sa yunit ng $t_h$ at ang oras sa yunit ng $1/t_h$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Real-time dynamics of this model are hard to compute classically. Exact diagonalization stops near $L \\lesssim 14$ sites, and after a quench, the entanglement entropy of a tensor-network solver grows linearly in time, so the bond dimension needed for fixed accuracy grows exponentially.\n"
msgstr "Mahirap kuwentahin nang classical ang real-time dynamics ng model na ito. Humihinto ang exact diagonalization malapit sa $L \\lesssim 14$ na site, at pagkatapos ng quench, linear na lumalaki sa oras ang entanglement entropy ng isang tensor-network solver, kaya exponential na lumalaki ang bond dimension na kailangan para sa nakatakdang accuracy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In one dimension, the elementary excitations are spinons, which carry spin and no charge, and holons, which carry charge and no spin. The two propagate at different speeds, so a localized disturbance splits into a fast front and a slow one. This effect is called spin-charge separation, and this tutorial measures it [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr "Sa isang dimensyon, ang mga elementary excitation ay ang mga spinon, na may dalang spin at walang charge, at ang mga holon, na may dalang charge at walang spin. Magkaiba ang bilis ng pagkalat ng dalawa, kaya nahahati ang isang naka-localize na gambala sa mabilis na front at mabagal na front. Tinatawag itong spin-charge separation, at sinusukat ito ng tutorial na ito [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses the Dynamics Simulator Qiskit Function, which takes the Hamiltonian, an initial state, a Trotter schedule, and a list of observables, and returns expectation values. It handles the Jordan-Wigner mapping, Trotterization, qubit layout, and error suppression internally, so there are no circuits to build or transpile in this tutorial.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang tutorial na ito ng Dynamics Simulator Qiskit Function, na tumatanggap ng Hamiltonian, isang initial state, isang Trotter schedule, at isang listahan ng mga observable, at nagbabalik ng mga expectation value. Ito na ang bahala sa Jordan-Wigner mapping, Trotterization, qubit layout, at error suppression sa loob, kaya walang circuit na bubuuin o ita-transpile sa tutorial na ito.\n"

