# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the Hamiltonian {#define-the-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "I-define ang Hamiltonian {#define-the-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function takes the model as a dictionary with three keys. Each one accepts either a single float, which applies uniformly along the chain, or a list that specifies the value site by site. Lists have $L-1$ entries for `hopping_amplitude`, because an open chain has one fewer bond than sites, and $L$ entries for `on_site_interaction` and `chemical_potential`.\n"
msgstr "Tinatanggap ng function ang model bilang dictionary na may tatlong key. Tumatanggap ang bawat isa ng isang float, na pantay na ilalapat sa buong chain, o isang listahan na tumutukoy sa halaga kada site. May $L-1$ na entry ang mga listahan para sa `hopping_amplitude`, dahil may isang bond na mas kaunti ang open chain kaysa sa bilang ng site, at $L$ na entry para sa `on_site_interaction` at `chemical_potential`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses a uniform chain of 31 sites with a repulsive interaction $U/t_h = 8$. A uniform chemical potential contributes only a global phase when the particle number is fixed, so this example sets it to zero. The chemical potential matters only when it varies from site to site, for example, to add disorder or a single impurity.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang tutorial na ito ng uniform na chain na 31 site na may repulsive interaction na $U/t_h = 8$. Global phase lang ang naiaambag ng uniform na chemical potential kapag nakapirmi ang bilang ng particle, kaya ginawa itong zero ng halimbawang ito. Mahalaga lang ang chemical potential kapag nag-iiba ito sa bawat site, halimbawa para magdagdag ng disorder o ng isang impurity.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the Trotter schedule {#set-the-trotter-schedule}"
msgstr "Itakda ang Trotter schedule {#set-the-trotter-schedule}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `simulation` dictionary holds the time step ($\\Delta t$) and the number of Trotter steps, and the total evolution time is their product. Larger steps reach later times at fixed circuit depth but incur more Trotter error, which grows with $U$ because the Hamiltonian terms commute less. The published hardware study used $\\Delta t = 0.15$ for $U/t_h = 8$ [\\[2\\]](#references), and this tutorial uses the same value. Circuit depth grows linearly in the step count and does not depend on $L$ at all.\n"
msgstr "Hawak ng `simulation` dictionary ang time step ($\\Delta t$) at ang bilang ng Trotter step, at ang kabuuang evolution time ay ang produkto nila. Mas malalayong oras ang naaabot ng mas malalaking step sa nakapirmi na circuit depth pero mas malaki ang Trotter error, na lumalaki kasabay ng $U$ dahil mas kaunti ang nagko-commute na term ng Hamiltonian. Gumamit ang nailathalang hardware study ng $\\Delta t = 0.15$ para sa $U/t_h = 8$ [\\[2\\]](#references), at ang parehong halaga ang ginagamit ng tutorial na ito. Linear na lumalaki ang circuit depth sa bilang ng step at hindi ito nakadepende sa $L$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the initial state {#prepare-the-initial-state}"
msgstr "Ihanda ang initial state {#prepare-the-initial-state}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each site holds two spin orbitals, so an $L$-site chain uses $2L$ qubits. The initial state is a Fock occupation string with one character per site:\n"
msgstr "May dalawang spin orbital ang bawat site, kaya $2L$ na qubit ang ginagamit ng chain na may $L$ site. Ang initial state ay isang Fock occupation string na may isang character kada site:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\texttt{empty (e)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (0,0), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{up (u)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (1,0), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{down (d)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (0,1), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{both (b)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (1,1).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\texttt{empty (e)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (0,0), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{up (u)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (1,0), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{down (d)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (0,1), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{both (b)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (1,1).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The string is read least significant site first, so the rightmost character is site 0 and the physical site index of character $k$ counted from the left is $i = L - 1 - k$. The string `udud` therefore means site 0 is `d`, site 1 is `u`, site 2 is `d`, and site 3 is `u`.\n"
msgstr "Binabasa ang string mula sa pinakamababang significant na site muna, kaya ang pinakakanang character ay site 0 at ang pisikal na site index ng character na $k$ na binibilang mula kaliwa ay $i = L - 1 - k$. Kaya ang string na `udud` ay nangangahulugang `d` ang site 0, `u` ang site 1, `d` ang site 2, at `u` ang site 3.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, prepare a half-filled Néel state, alternating `u` and `d`, with the central site replaced by a vacancy. The vacancy is the disturbance whose spreading is tracked.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, ihanda ang half-filled na Néel state, na salitan ang `u` at `d`, kung saan pinalitan ng vacancy ang gitnang site. Ang vacancy ang gambalang susundan ang pagkalat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the observables {#build-the-observables}"
msgstr "Buuin ang mga observable {#build-the-observables}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each observable is a dictionary that represents a weighted sum of products of occupation operators:\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat observable ay isang dictionary na kumakatawan sa weighted sum ng mga produkto ng occupation operator:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"O = \\sum_{\\alpha} c_{\\alpha} \\prod_{(\\sigma, j) \\in T_{\\alpha}} n_{j,\\sigma}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"O = \\sum_{\\alpha} c_{\\alpha} \\prod_{(\\sigma, j) \\in T_{\\alpha}} n_{j,\\sigma}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every entry of `operators` is one term $T_{\\alpha}$, written as a list of `[name, site]` pairs that multiply together, and the matching entry of `coefficients` is its weight. The two names are `\"Nup\"` for $n_{j,\\uparrow}$ and `\"Ndn\"` for $n_{j,\\downarrow}$. A single one-point observable $n_{3,\\uparrow}$ is written as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat entry ng `operators` ay isang term na $T_{\\alpha}$, na isinulat bilang listahan ng mga pares na `[name, site]` na pinaparami, at ang katumbas na entry ng `coefficients` ang timbang nito. Ang dalawang pangalan ay `\"Nup\"` para sa $n_{j,\\uparrow}$ at `\"Ndn\"` para sa $n_{j,\\downarrow}$. Ganito isinusulat ang isang one-point observable na $n_{3,\\uparrow}$:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next cell prints the smallest complete set of inputs the function accepts, which is useful as a shape reference while reading the code that follows.\n"
msgstr "Ipi-print ng susunod na cell ang pinakamaliit na kumpletong set ng mga input na tinatanggap ng function, na kapaki-pakinabang bilang sanggunian sa hugis habang binabasa ang code na kasunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three groups of observables are needed. The charge density $n_i = n_{i\\uparrow} + n_{i\\downarrow}$ and the local spin $S^z_i = (n_{i\\uparrow} - n_{i\\downarrow})/2$ are both two-term sums over the same operators, differing only in their coefficients. The spin correlator $S^z_i S^z_{i_*}$ between site $i$ and the vacancy site expands into four two-point terms with coefficients $\\pm 1/4$.\n"
msgstr "Tatlong grupo ng mga observable ang kailangan. Ang charge density na $n_i = n_{i\\uparrow} + n_{i\\downarrow}$ at ang local spin na $S^z_i = (n_{i\\uparrow} - n_{i\\downarrow})/2$ ay parehong two-term sum sa iisang mga operator, na magkaiba lang sa mga coefficient. Ang spin correlator na $S^z_i S^z_{i_*}$ sa pagitan ng site $i$ at ng vacancy site ay lumalawak sa apat na two-point term na may mga coefficient na $\\pm 1/4$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Occupation operators commute, so the order of factors within a term is irrelevant, but the order of the `observables` list fixes the order of the returned values. The code records an index for each group while it builds the list. The correlator skips the vacancy site, where the product would repeat a factor.\n"
msgstr "Nagko-commute ang mga occupation operator, kaya walang epekto ang ayos ng mga factor sa loob ng isang term, pero ang ayos ng listahan ng `observables` ang nagtatakda ng ayos ng mga ibinabalik na halaga. Nagre-record ang code ng index para sa bawat grupo habang binubuo ang listahan. Nilalaktawan ng correlator ang vacancy site, kung saan uulitin ng produkto ang isang factor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pag-execute sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial has no transpilation step. The function performs the following steps internally [\\[2\\]](#references), and you cannot configure them from the notebook:\n"
msgstr "Walang transpilation step ang tutorial na ito. Ginagawa ng function ang mga sumusunod na hakbang sa loob [\\[2\\]](#references), at hindi mo ito ma-configure mula sa notebook:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Maps the fermionic modes to qubits under an ordering chosen to keep Pauli weights low on a heavy-hex lattice\n"
msgstr "Minamapa ang mga fermionic mode sa mga qubit sa ayos na pinili para panatilihing mababa ang Pauli weight sa heavy-hex lattice\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Uses a fermionic SWAP network so every hopping term becomes a two-qubit rotation\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ng fermionic SWAP network para maging two-qubit rotation ang bawat hopping term\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Embeds the chain along a path that avoids weak qubits\n"
msgstr "Inilalagay ang chain sa isang landas na umiiwas sa mahihinang qubit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applies dynamical decoupling and Pauli twirling during compilation\n"
msgstr "Naglalapat ng dynamical decoupling at Pauli twirling habang nagko-compile\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You choose the backend and the shot count. The function takes a backend name as a string, so this tutorial selects the least busy device large enough for the chain and passes its name.\n"
msgstr "Ikaw ang pipili ng backend at ng bilang ng shot. Tumatanggap ang function ng pangalan ng backend bilang string, kaya pinipili ng tutorial na ito ang device na pinakamaluwag ang pila at sapat ang laki para sa chain, at ipinapasa ang pangalan nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The smallest signal that you need to resolve sets the shot count. The charge tracer reaches amplitudes near $0.15$, but the connected spin tracer peaks around $0.04$, roughly four times smaller. The published study used 20,000 shots per circuit for this reason [\\[2\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr "Ang pinakamaliit na signal na kailangan mong makita ang nagtatakda ng bilang ng shot. Umaabot ang charge tracer sa mga amplitude na malapit sa $0.15$, pero ang connected spin tracer ay pumipinakto sa paligid ng $0.04$, halos apat na beses na mas maliit. Dahil dito, gumamit ang nailathalang pag-aaral ng 20,000 shot kada circuit [\\[2\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute by using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-by-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Step 3: I-execute gamit ang Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-by-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, submit the simulation. `run` returns a job handle immediately rather than blocking.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, i-submit ang simulation. Agad na nagbabalik ng job handle ang `run` sa halip na maghintay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use `job.status()` to follow progress and `job.result()` to block until the job finishes. The result is a mapping whose `observable_expectation_values` entry is indexed first by observable, in the order they were supplied, and then by time. There are `step_count + 1` time points because the value at $t=0$ is included.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang `job.status()` para subaybayan ang progreso at ang `job.result()` para maghintay hanggang matapos ang job. Ang result ay isang mapping na ang entry na `observable_expectation_values` ay naka-index muna ayon sa observable, sa ayos na ibinigay ang mga ito, at pagkatapos ay ayon sa oras. May `step_count + 1` na time point dahil kasama ang halaga sa $t=0$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Step 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang result sa nais na classical na format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reconstruct the correlators {#reconstruct-the-correlators}"
msgstr "Buuin muli ang mga correlator {#reconstruct-the-correlators}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Split the flat array back into the three groups using the indices recorded earlier, then form the two tracer correlators. The charge tracer is the change in per-site density relative to $t=0$:\n"
msgstr "Hatiin muli ang flat array sa tatlong grupo gamit ang mga indices na naitala kanina, tapos buuin ang dalawang tracer correlator. Ang charge tracer ay ang pagbabago sa density kada site kumpara sa $t=0$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C^c_i(t) = \\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(t) + n_{i\\downarrow}(t) \\rangle - \\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(0) + n_{i\\downarrow}(0) \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C^c_i(t) = \\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(t) + n_{i\\downarrow}(t) \\rangle - \\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(0) + n_{i\\downarrow}(0) \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The spin tracer is the connected correlator between each site and the vacancy site $i_*$:\n"
msgstr "Ang spin tracer ay ang connected correlator sa pagitan ng bawat site at ng vacancy site na $i_*$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C^s_i(t) = 4 \\left( \\langle S^z_i S^z_{i_*} \\rangle - \\langle S^z_i \\rangle \\langle S^z_{i_*} \\rangle \\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C^s_i(t) = 4 \\left( \\langle S^z_i S^z_{i_*} \\rangle - \\langle S^z_i \\rangle \\langle S^z_{i_*} \\rangle \\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both are built from Fock-basis operators, so they come from the same measured bitstrings and the second one costs no extra hardware execution.\n"
msgstr "Parehong buo mula sa mga operator sa Fock-basis, kaya galing sila sa parehong mga sinukat na bitstring at hindi na kailangan ng dagdag na hardware execution para sa pangalawa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you constructed the observables, the code recorded the position of each charge (`charge_indices`), spin (`spin_indices`), and spin-correlation (`correlator_indices`) operator in the list. Because the simulator returns the expectation values in the same order, you can use these positions to extract the corresponding results. For the spin correlations, the code also uses `correlator_sites` to place each result at the correct lattice position, and leaves the vacancy as `NaN`.\n"
msgstr "Noong binuo mo ang mga observable, itinala ng code ang posisyon ng bawat charge (`charge_indices`), spin (`spin_indices`), at spin-correlation (`correlator_indices`) na operator sa listahan. Dahil ibinabalik ng simulator ang mga expectation value sa parehong pagkakasunod-sunod, magagamit mo ang mga posisyong ito para kunin ang kaukulang mga resulta. Para sa mga spin correlation, ginagamit din ng code ang `correlator_sites` para ilagay ang bawat resulta sa tamang posisyon sa lattice, at iniiwang `NaN` ang vacancy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the wavefronts {#visualize-the-wavefronts}"
msgstr "I-visualize ang mga wavefront {#visualize-the-wavefronts}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you plot each correlator as a heatmap of space and time, the light cone is directly visible. Time flows downward, and the horizontal axis is the position along the chain.\n"
msgstr "Kapag ipinlot mo ang bawat correlator bilang heatmap ng espasyo at oras, direktang makikita ang light cone. Pababa ang daloy ng oras, at ang pahalang na axis ay ang posisyon sa kahabaan ng chain.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c75549b7-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c75549b7-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extract the wavefront velocities {#extract-the-wavefront-velocities}"
msgstr "Kunin ang mga velocity ng wavefront {#extract-the-wavefront-velocities}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Turn the heatmaps into numbers by following the detection protocol from the published study [\\[2\\]](#references). At each time slice, symmetrize the spatial profile about the vacancy, which averages away the antisymmetric part of the hardware noise, normalize by the largest off-center amplitude, and record the outermost site above a threshold. Detections are then cut into runs of consecutive time steps, and only the longest run is fit, which keeps the early-time transient out of the result.\n"
msgstr "Gawing mga numero ang mga heatmap sa pamamagitan ng pagsunod sa detection protocol mula sa nailathalang pag-aaral [\\[2\\]](#references). Sa bawat time slice, i-symmetrize ang spatial profile sa paligid ng vacancy, na nag-a-average palabas sa antisymmetric na bahagi ng hardware noise, i-normalize gamit ang pinakamalaking off-center na amplitude, at itala ang pinakalabas na site na lampas sa threshold. Pagkatapos, hinihiwa ang mga detection sa mga run ng magkakasunod na time step, at ang pinakamahabang run lang ang fi-nifit, para hindi mapasama sa resulta ang early-time transient.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The fitted velocity depends on the detection threshold and the trimming quantile, and that sensitivity dominates the shot noise. Scan both and report the median with the full envelope, as the published analysis does.\n"
msgstr "Nakadepende ang fitted velocity sa detection threshold at sa trimming quantile, at mas malaki ang epekto ng sensitivity na iyon kaysa sa shot noise. I-scan ang dalawa at iulat ang median kasama ang buong envelope, gaya ng ginagawa sa nailathalang analysis.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/640db359-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/640db359-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Drawing the detections back onto the heatmaps shows whether the algorithm tracked\n"
"the leading edge. Filled markers are the detections that entered\n"
"the fit. Open markers were cut by the masking rules, either because they sit too\n"
"close to the vacancy, too close to the chain end, or were late enough that the front has\n"
"broadened and its position is no longer sharp. The dashed line is the fit over the\n"
"times it used, and its slope is the velocity in each panel title.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag ibinalik sa mga heatmap ang mga detection, makikita kung nasundan ng algorithm\n"
"ang leading edge. Ang mga filled marker ay ang mga detection na napasama\n"
"sa fit. Ang mga open marker ay inalis ng mga masking rule, dahil masyado silang malapit\n"
"sa vacancy, masyadong malapit sa dulo ng chain, o huli na kaya ang front ay\n"
"lumapad na at hindi na malinaw ang posisyon nito. Ang dashed line ay ang fit sa mga\n"
"oras na ginamit nito, at ang slope nito ang velocity sa title ng bawat panel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The vacancy column is marked below the axis. The charge clips there because its value\n"
"is of order one, and spin has no value there, so it is drawn in gray.\n"
msgstr ""
"Minarkahan sa ilalim ng axis ang column ng vacancy. Na-clip doon ang charge dahil ang halaga nito\n"
"ay nasa order na isa, at walang halaga ang spin doon, kaya kulay gray ang pagkaguhit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The charge cone opens wider than the spin cone. Both disturbances leave the same\n"
"defect at the same moment and travel outward at different speeds.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mas malawak ang bukas ng charge cone kaysa sa spin cone. Iniiwan ng dalawang disturbance ang parehong\n"
"defect sa parehong sandali at naglalakbay palabas sa magkaibang bilis.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/25192e92-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/25192e92-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The charge front outruns the spin front. A hole in a one-dimensional Mott background does not travel as an electron. Instead, it fractionalizes into a holon carrying the charge and a spinon carrying the spin disturbance, and at $U/t_h = 8$ the spinon is the slower of the two.\n"
msgstr "Nauuna ang charge front sa spin front. Ang isang hole sa one-dimensional na Mott background ay hindi naglalakbay bilang isang electron. Sa halip, nahahati ito sa isang holon na may dalang charge at isang spinon na may dalang spin disturbance, at sa $U/t_h = 8$ ang spinon ang mas mabagal sa dalawa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ordering depends on the interaction. At $U = 0$, the model is free fermions with $v_c = 2$ and $v_s = 4$, so spin is faster. Repulsion suppresses spin transport while leaving charge transport nearly untouched, and by $U/t_h = 8$ the published hardware values are $v_c = 1.78$ and $v_s = 1.46$ [\\[2\\]](#references). Rerunning with several values of $U$ and plotting $v_s / v_c$ maps the crossover.\n"
msgstr "Nakadepende ang pagkakasunod-sunod sa interaction. Sa $U = 0$, ang model ay mga free fermion na may $v_c = 2$ at $v_s = 4$, kaya mas mabilis ang spin. Pinipigilan ng repulsion ang spin transport habang halos hindi ginagalaw ang charge transport, at pagdating ng $U/t_h = 8$, ang mga nailathalang halaga mula sa hardware ay $v_c = 1.78$ at $v_s = 1.46$ [\\[2\\]](#references). Kapag inulit ang run gamit ang ilang halaga ng $U$ at ipinlot ang $v_s / v_c$, makikita ang crossover.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note these caveats on the numbers. Threshold-based detection is biased slightly low, so a charge velocity a few percent under the published value is expected. The spin envelope is wide because the connected correlator sits closer to the noise floor, which is why the median of the scan rather than a single fit is quoted.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan ang mga caveat na ito sa mga numero. Bahagyang mababa ang bias ng threshold-based detection, kaya inaasahan ang charge velocity na ilang porsiyentong mas mababa sa nailathalang halaga. Malapad ang spin envelope dahil mas malapit sa noise floor ang connected correlator, kaya ang median ng scan ang binabanggit sa halip na isang fit lang.\n"

